# The loop of a gallop: `last = offset; offset = (offset * 2 + 1) | 0; if (offset > most) offset = most;`: through a join an operator on bits and an int32 made in front of the loop come round as `offset`, and `offset` itself as `last`. It was walked four times: `offset` misfitted, then `last`, then the walk that fitted was walked again for the narrower form.
# Both start as int32: one walk, none undone.
# -- source: what-operators-on-bits-and-another-such-parameter-bring-round-starts-as-int32.cjs
